## 5. Graceful Shutdown & Uncaught Exceptions

To avoid dangling processes or data loss, handle `SIGTERM`, `SIGINT`, and `unhandledRejection`/`uncaughtException`.

```js
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
  // decide whether to shut down or keep running
});

process.on('uncaughtException', (err) => {
  console.error('Uncaught Exception:', err);
  process.exit(1); // crash fast, let orchestrator restart
});

const server = app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server listening on ${PORT}`);
});

process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  console.log('SIGTERM received – closing server');
  server.close(() => process.exit(0));
});
```

