## 1. Harden the HTTP stack  

| Issue | Why it matters | Recommended fix |
|-------|----------------|-----------------|
| **No security‑headers middleware** | Browsers will accept the default, which leaves the app vulnerable to click‑jacking, MIME‑sniffing, XSS, etc. | Install and use **helmet**: `app.use(require('helmet')());` |
| **No CORS policy** | By default every origin can call your API, which may not be what you want. | Add `cors` with a whitelist: `app.use(require('cors')({ origin: allowedOrigins }));` |
| **No rate limiting** | Allows brute‑force / DoS attacks on any endpoint (including `/health`). | Use `express-rate-limit` (e.g. 100 req / 15 min per IP). |
| **No HTTPS enforcement** | If the app is ever exposed over HTTP, credentials can be sniffed. | In production, add `app.use((req, res, next) => { if (req.secure) return next(); res.redirect(\`https://\${req.headers.host}\${req.url}\`); });` or rely on a reverse‑proxy. |

