// … define routes …
app.use(errorHandler);
```

### b) Async‑wrapper for route handlers
If you later add any asynchronous logic (DB calls, external APIs) you’ll want a helper that catches rejected promises automatically:

```js
// asyncWrapper.js
const asyncWrapper = fn => (req, res, next) => {
